== the curve and its flexes
ok  [0:1:0] is not on C (projection from it is defined on C)
ok  Res_y(F, Hess)(x, 1) has degree 24 and is irreducible over Q
ok  no flex on the line z = 0 (F(1,y,0) has degree 4 in y and [0:1:0] is not on C)
   so the 24 flexes are distinct, simple zeros of Hess on C (Hess.C = sum of the 24 flexes), with distinct x/z
== the algebra A3
ok  disc(O_A3) = -2^8 7^9, so A3 is unramified outside 2, 7
ok  signature (2, 3)
ok  A3 has no subfield other than Q and A3
  *** nfsplitting: Warning: increasing stack size to 16000000.
ok  the Galois closure of A3 has degree 336 (nfsplitting)
ok  Frobenius cycle types 7+1 (p = 193) and 8 (p = 199) occur
   hence Gal = the transitive group of degree 8 and order 336, 8T43 = PGL(2,7) (GAP: twodesc_1_module.g)
ok  A3 = Q[X]/Phi_7(X, 12544) (the 7-isogeny field of E3, j(E3) = 12544)
== the triangle over A3
ok  Res_y(F, Hess)(x,1) has a cubic factor cT over A3
ok  Norm_{A3/Q}(cT) = Res_y(F,Hess)(x,1)/lc: the 8 conjugate triples partition the 24 flexes
ok  y = YT(x) has degree exactly 2 on the triple: its three flexes are not collinear
ok  the flex T1 has contact order >= 3 with its tangent
ok  the fourth point of the tangent at T1 is a flex of the same triple (triangle)
ok     and its y-coordinate is YT(x) of that flex
ok     and it is not T1 itself
   hence 4T ~ 3H for every triangle T (the product of the three tangent lines meets C in 4T)
== the cubic G_A
ok  the cubics over A3 with order >= 3 at P0 and contact >= 2 at the three flexes of T form a line
GA = Mod(-182126*a^7 + 116484*a^6 + 189401*a^5 - 863261*a^4 + 21839*a^3 + 2573121*a^2 + 961083*a - 2273080, a^8 + 2*a^7 + 7*a^4 - 14*a^2 - 8*a + 5)*x^3 + (Mod(-122607*a^7 - 902587*a^6 - 827093*a^5 + 444073*a^4 - 1067727*a^3 - 2132803*a^2 + 4020006*a + 6034815, a^8 + 2*a^7 + 7*a^4 - 14*a^2 - 8*a + 5)*y + Mod(299190*a^7 + 648290*a^6 - 448940*a^5 + 387340*a^4 + 1898340*a^3 - 1693240*a^2 - 4402770*a + 3198325, a^8 + 2*a^7 + 7*a^4 - 14*a^2 - 8*a + 5)*z)*x^2 + (Mod(85965*a^7 + 1315440*a^6 - 221340*a^5 - 1260010*a^4 + 3048490*a^3 + 2996360*a^2 - 5068845*a + 608450, a^8 + 2*a^7 + 7*a^4 - 14*a^2 - 8*a + 5)*y^2 + Mod(798325*a^7 + 2038825*a^6 - 318950*a^5 + 803450*a^4 + 4795950*a^3 - 2831700*a^2 - 12848475*a - 6854625, a^8 + 2*a^7 + 7*a^4 - 14*a^2 - 8*a + 5)*z*y + Mod(2098750, a^8 + 2*a^7 + 7*a^4 - 14*a^2 - 8*a + 5)*z^2)*x + (Mod(242050*a^7 + 1060300*a^6 - 1380800*a^5 - 493700*a^4 + 3751300*a^3 - 506800*a^2 - 5302650*a - 1178500, a^8 + 2*a^7 + 7*a^4 - 14*a^2 - 8*a + 5)*y^3 + Mod(125875*a^7 + 1045250*a^6 + 2008500*a^5 - 412250*a^4 + 125250*a^3 + 3503500*a^2 - 4603875*a - 9580000, a^8 + 2*a^7 + 7*a^4 - 14*a^2 - 8*a + 5)*z*y^2 + 5246875*z^2*y)
ok  Res_y(F, GA) is a binary form of degree 12 with nonzero x^12 coefficient: no point of C.G on z = 0
ok  exponent of x in Res_y(F, GA) is 3: I_P0(C, G) = 3 and no other point of C on x = 0 lies on G
ok  exponent of cT is 2: I_T(C, G) = 2 at each flex of T, no other point above those x lies on G
ok  the residual factor is a cubic with rational coefficients
   r3 = 1633*x^3 - 4901*x^2 + 3500*x + 6250
ok  r3 is irreducible over Q
ok  r3 is prime to x and to the flex polynomial
ok  above each root of r3 exactly one point of C lies on all conjugates of G
ok  R = (u, yR(u), 1), r3(u) = 0, lies on C
ok  GA vanishes at R over A3 (x) Q(u): R is a Q-rational divisor, the same for all conjugates of G
   R: x = u, y = 1633/3115*u^2 - 5617/6230*u + 375/1246, z = 1, with u^3 - 4901/1633*u^2 + 3500/1633*u + 6250/1633 = 0
ok  the three points of R are not collinear
   => div(G_omega) = 2 T_omega + E for every omega in Omega, with E = 3 P0 + R a Q-rational divisor
== the cubic Psi with div(Psi) = 2E = 6 P0 + 2R
ok  the cubics over Q with order >= 6 at P0 and contact >= 2 at R form a line
   Psi = -161*x^3 + (110*y + 52*z)*x^2 + (-225*y^2 - 327*z*y + 92*z^2)*x + (-522*y^3 + 65*z*y^2 + 230*z^2*y)
ok  no point of C.Psi on z = 0
ok  Res_y(F, Psi) = const * x^6 * r3^2: div(Psi) = 6 P0 + 2R exactly
   => 2E ~ 3H; with 2T + E ~ 3H this gives 4T ~ 3H again, and sum_omega T_omega = Hess.C ~ 6H ~ 8 T_omega0
== norm identity N_{A3/Q}(G_A) = c * Hess^2 * Psi^4 modulo F
ok  P1 = (1,1,1) is on C
ok  N(GA) - c Hess^2 Psi^4 is divisible by F, c = [-1, 1; 2, -2; 3, -6; 5, 28; 7, -3; 23, 6; 73, 8]
   => for every degree 0 divisor D disjoint from the supports, N(delta(D)) = Hess(D)^2 Psi(D)^4 is a square
== P0 and the Hessian: supports
ok  P0 is not a flex
step 1 done
